    {"ID": 398, "Category": "Technology", "Specialty": "IT", "Difficulty": "Easy", "Question": "What components are needed to set up a Basic Home Network?", "Answer": "A basic home network requires a router or hub, LAN cards, and LAN cables to connect devices for internet and local network access."},
    {"ID": 399, "Category": "Technology", "Specialty": "IT", "Difficulty": "Hard", "Question": "What is the purpose of BOOT.INI?", "Answer": "BOOT.INI is a configuration file in older Windows versions used to define which operating system options are displayed during the boot-up process."},
    {"ID": 400, "Category": "Technology", "Specialty": "IT", "Difficulty": "Medium", "Question": "Identify a few types of Firewalls.", "Answer": "There are two main types: network layer firewalls, which filter traffic based on source and destination addresses, and application layer firewalls, which operate on proxy servers. Examples include Comodo and ZoneAlarm."},
    {"ID": 401, "Category": "Technology", "Specialty": "IT", "Difficulty": "Medium", "Question": "How would you handle a situation where a critical system is down and needs urgent attention?", "Answer": "I would follow an incident response plan, immediately assess the issue, communicate with stakeholders, prioritize resolution, document the root cause, and implement preventive measures."},
    {"ID": 402, "Category": "Technology", "Specialty": "IT", "Difficulty": "Easy", "Question": "What is the purpose of a VPN, and when would you use it?", "Answer": "A VPN (Virtual Private Network) encrypts internet traffic to enhance security and privacy, commonly used for remote work or accessing restricted networks."},
    {"ID": 403, "Category": "Technology", "Specialty": "IT", "Difficulty": "Hard", "Question": "Explain the difference between scalability and elasticity in cloud computing.", "Answer": "Scalability refers to increasing system capacity over time, while elasticity automatically adjusts resources dynamically based on real-time demand."},
    {"ID": 404, "Category": "Technology", "Specialty": "IT", "Difficulty": "Medium", "Question": "How would you optimize network performance in an enterprise environment?", "Answer": "I would use network monitoring tools, configure QoS, optimize bandwidth allocation, implement caching, and minimize latency through efficient routing."},
    {"ID": 405, "Category": "Technology", "Specialty": "IT", "Difficulty": "Easy", "Question": "What is a MAC address, and how does it differ from an IP address?", "Answer": "A MAC address is a unique identifier for a network device, while an IP address is assigned for communication across networks and can change dynamically."},
    {"ID": 406, "Category": "Technology", "Specialty": "IT", "Difficulty": "Medium", "Question": "What steps would you take to secure a wireless network?", "Answer": "I would use strong encryption (WPA3), disable SSID broadcasting, implement MAC filtering, update firmware, and monitor for unauthorized access."},
    {"ID": 407, "Category": "Technology", "Specialty": "IT", "Difficulty": "Medium", "Question": "What is an IT service catalog, and how does it benefit an organization?", "Answer": "An IT service catalog provides a structured list of IT services, helping organizations standardize service requests and improve IT service management."},
    {"ID": 408, "Category": "Technology", "Specialty": "IT", "Difficulty": "Hard", "Question": "How do you secure an Internet of Things (IoT) environment?", "Answer": "I use network segmentation, strong authentication, firmware updates, and device monitoring to mitigate IoT-related risks."},
    {"ID": 409, "Category": "Technology", "Specialty": "IT", "Difficulty": "Easy", "Question": "What is IT governance, and why is it important?", "Answer": "IT governance ensures that IT processes align with business objectives, regulatory requirements, and risk management strategies."},
    {"ID": 410, "Category": "Technology", "Specialty": "IT", "Difficulty": "Medium", "Question": "What is an endpoint security solution, and why is it important?", "Answer": "Endpoint security protects devices like laptops and mobile phones from cyber threats, ensuring compliance and preventing unauthorized access to sensitive data."},
    {"ID": 411, "Category": "Technology", "Specialty": "IT", "Difficulty": "Easy", "Question": "What is a service-level agreement (SLA), and why is it important?", "Answer": "An SLA defines the expected level of service between a provider and a client, ensuring accountability, performance standards, and resolution timelines."},
    {"ID": 412, "Category": "Technology", "Specialty": "IT", "Difficulty": "Hard", "Question": "How would you handle a data breach in an organization?", "Answer": "I would isolate affected systems, assess the scope of the breach, notify relevant stakeholders, enhance security measures, and conduct a post-incident review to prevent recurrence."},
    {"ID": 413, "Category": "Technology", "Specialty": "IT", "Difficulty": "Medium", "Question": "What is the importance of IT compliance and regulatory frameworks?", "Answer": "Compliance ensures organizations adhere to legal standards like GDPR, HIPAA, and ISO 27001, protecting data and reducing security risks."},
    {"ID": 414, "Category": "Technology", "Specialty": "IT", "Difficulty": "Easy", "Question": "What is a domain controller, and what role does it play in a network?", "Answer": "A domain controller manages authentication, user permissions, and security policies in a Windows Active Directory environment."},
    {"ID": 415, "Category": "Technology", "Specialty": "IT", "Difficulty": "Hard", "Question": "What is a honeypot in cybersecurity, and how is it used?", "Answer": "A honeypot is a decoy system designed to lure attackers, helping organizations detect threats, analyze attack patterns, and improve security defenses."},
    {"ID": 416, "Category": "Technology", "Specialty": "IT", "Difficulty": "Easy", "Question": "What is a botnet attack, and how can organizations defend against it?", "Answer": "A botnet attack uses compromised devices to execute cyberattacks. Organizations can prevent this through network monitoring, endpoint security, and firewall controls."},
    {"ID": 417, "Category": "Technology", "Specialty": "IT", "Difficulty": "Easy", "Question": "What is two-factor authentication (2FA), and why is it recommended?", "Answer": "2FA adds an extra layer of security by requiring a second form of authentication, such as a one-time code or biometric verification, reducing unauthorized access risks."},
    {"ID": 418, "Category": "Technology", "Specialty": "IT", "Difficulty": "Hard", "Question": "What is Zero Trust security, and how does it differ from traditional security models?", "Answer": "Zero Trust assumes no inherent trust within the network, requiring continuous authentication and least-privilege access compared to perimeter-based security models."},
    {"ID": 419, "Category": "Technology", "Specialty": "IT", "Difficulty": "Medium", "Question": "What is the difference between a software-defined network (SDN) and a traditional network?", "Answer": "SDN centralizes network control, improving automation and flexibility, while traditional networks rely on manual configuration and hardware-based management."},
    {"ID": 420, "Category": "Technology", "Specialty": "IT", "Difficulty": "Easy", "Question": "What is phishing, and how can users protect themselves?", "Answer": "Phishing is a cyberattack tricking users into providing sensitive data via deceptive emails or websites. Users should verify sources, avoid clicking unknown links, and use security tools."},
    {"ID": 421, "Category": "Technology", "Specialty": "IT", "Difficulty": "Easy", "Question": "How would you explain the difference between front-end and back-end development?", "Answer": "Front-end development focuses on the user interface and experience, while back-end development handles server-side logic, databases, and application functionality."},
    {"ID": 422, "Category": "Technology", "Specialty": "IT", "Difficulty": "Medium", "Question": "How do you assess the security vulnerabilities of an organization's IT infrastructure?", "Answer": "I conduct vulnerability scans, penetration testing, security audits, and implement continuous monitoring to detect and mitigate threats."},
    {"ID": 423, "Category": "Technology", "Specialty": "IT", "Difficulty": "Easy", "Question": "What is a virtual desktop infrastructure (VDI), and what are its benefits?", "Answer": "VDI allows users to access a virtualized desktop environment remotely, improving security, scalability, and device flexibility."},
    {"ID": 424, "Category": "Technology", "Specialty": "IT", "Difficulty": "Hard", "Question": "How do you implement a network segmentation strategy?", "Answer": "I divide networks into separate subnets based on roles, enforce access controls, use VLANs, and apply firewall rules to minimize attack surfaces."},
    {"ID": 425, "Category": "Technology", "Specialty": "IT", "Difficulty": "Medium", "Question": "What is a shadow IT system, and how can organizations mitigate its risks?", "Answer": "Shadow IT refers to unauthorized applications or devices used within an organization. It can be mitigated by enforcing policies, increasing user awareness, and implementing IT monitoring tools."},
